!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# convex
# `convex/_generated/` and `convex/betterAuth/_generated/` are deliberately NOT
# ignored. They are derived — `bunx convex dev` rewrites them from the schema
# and the function signatures — but they cannot be *re*-derived without
# credentials, which is the whole reason they are committed:
#
#   bunx convex codegen  →  "✖ No CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT set"
#
# and with a deployment name it still needs access to that project, because the
# full `api.d.ts` and the Better Auth component's `component.ts` are built from
# a deployment's own analysis of the pushed modules, not from the source alone.
# Convex's CLI says so itself: "This code is generated automatically while
# running `npx convex dev` and should be committed to the repo (your code won't
# typecheck without it!)".
#
# Ignoring them meant a clean checkout could not typecheck (46 `tsc` errors) and
# could not run the Convex tests (5 suites failing to import `./_generated/
# server`), so CI and any new contributor needed a Convex login before the gates
# would run at all. See the note in webapp/README.md on regenerating them.
.convex/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
